<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acadians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Acadians are the descendants of French colonists who settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>, in what are now the Maritime provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, from the 17th century. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> took the region in 1713, most tried to remain neutral, but from 1755 to 1764 the British deported more than 10,000 of them in the Great Upheaval. Many later returned to the Maritimes, while others settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>, where they became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cajuns">Cajuns</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/acadians.jpg" alt="Acadians" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Francois Arseneau (PD), referencing openclipart.org (by user Anonymous); modified by Krun. Own work based on: Fl... · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Acadia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
